Ticket #4471 holds **412 unique reports** (the export has 427 rows; 15 are repeats of the same
id). They are not one bug. Grouped by tenant locale and booking form, they are three.

<Callout>
The queued fix covers problem 1 only. Problems 2 and 3 have no ticket of their own until now.
</Callout>

## The three problems

| # | Problem | Reports | Where |
|---|---------|---------|-------|
| 1 ([#1](https://github.com/wojkos/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/1)) | The shared parser reads dates month first; day-first tenants' dates flip | 379 | all 11 tenants |
| 2 ([#2](https://github.com/wojkos/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/2)) | The `booking-v3` form hints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants, and reads their input day first | 33 | copper.studio, alder.physio, pale.harbour (form channel) |
| 3 ([#3](https://github.com/wojkos/kb-4471-what-it-shows/issues/3)) | Dates off by exactly one day (not a day/month flip), likely time zone or DST | 5 | R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620 |

Counts are what the kb cause table shows: parser 379 and hint 33 add up to the 412 unique reports. The 5 one-day reports are the cause table's footnote: the desk files them under the parser, so they are also inside the 379.

## How the reports were told apart

- The intake tag is a guess from the browser. It disagrees with the cause for 38 reports (23 tagged `hint` are really the parser; 15 tagged `parser` are really the hint). Do not triage by it.
- The 5 one-day reports were footnoted under the parser in `desk-notes.json`. A month flip cannot move a date by one day, so they are counted as their own problem here.
- The cause depends on the tenant: its locale, and which booking form it runs (`causes.ts`).

## Why it was merged as one

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. Subjects like
"Date is wrong" fit all three problems. "Splitting a ticket later is cheaper" holds only if someone
splits it; here nobody did for months.

## Tickets

Issue #1 (parser, 379), issue #2 (hint, 33, the cause that had no ticket) and issue #3 (one-day move, 5, also counted in the 379), each split from #4471.

